      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Based on existing research, individuals from East Asian backgrounds (e.g., Chinese, Japanese, Korean) tend to exhibit more verbal and analytical coping strategies, often manifested as hard work and long hours to excel in high-pressure professional settings. Mediterraneans, on the other hand, are often characterized by their flexibility, adaptability, and people-oriented approach, leading to more casual and extroverted behaviors in stressful situations. Additionally, East Asians may prioritize intellectual approach and masking negative emotions, while Mediterraneans may express emotions more openly. These differences can impact their teamwork, communication, and conflict resolution in professional settings.",
